       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, hyponatremia, and seizures, and they haven't been shown to work better. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that limit.\n\nYou could do one of these:\n- **Enter the usual dosing.** Start at 50 mg PO once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg/day. I can enter 200 mg PO daily now if that's the target.\n- **Confirm 400 mg is intended.** If it's deliberate, for example a specialist-directed regimen, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I can enter it flagged as above the labeled maximum, though pharmacy will probably still want to verify it.\n- **Fix a typo.** If you meant 40 mg or 100 mg, give me the correct dose and I'll enter it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
